meta {
  name: Connector Credentials - Set Default
  type: http
  seq: 10
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/v1/workspaces/:workspace/connector-credentials/:connectorCredential/default
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:path {
  workspace: {{workspaceId}}
  connectorCredential: {{connectorCredentialId}}
}

docs {
  Marks this credential as the one a node/agent gets when nothing pins a
  `credential_id` for its connector — Gumloop's "Personal Default"/"Use
  Team Default" auto-selection. Requires `connector.manage`.

  Unsets any previous default in the same group first, so at most one
  credential is ever the default per (connector, scope[, creator for a
  `personal` credential]) — setting a new default silently replaces the
  old one rather than erroring.

  If a connector has exactly one credential in a group, it's treated as
  that group's default automatically even without calling this — this
  endpoint matters once there's more than one to choose from.

  Response is wrapped:
  `{ success, statusCode, message, data: { connector_credential } }`.
}
